WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.458
A digital footprint is the information created, collected, or exposed through online activity,

00:00:05.458 --> 00:00:09.167
accounts, connected devices, services, public records, and technical infrastructure.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:14.112
It includes obvious material such as a public profile and less visible

00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:16.173
traces such as service logs,

00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:17.822
metadata, and indexed records.

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:22.767
An active footprint comes from deliberate sharing: posts, comments, uploads, resumes, websites,

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.004
or public code.

00:00:24.004 --> 00:00:28.125
A passive footprint is collected or exposed as activity occurs,

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.598
sometimes without a clear publishing decision.

00:00:30.598 --> 00:00:33.895
Examples include tracking records, technical logs, search indexes,

00:00:33.895 --> 00:00:36.368
and data held by third parties.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:39.665
Footprints can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical.

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:42.550
A professional profile may reveal work history.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.671
An organization may expose domains, job postings, documents, and partners.

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:50.792
Technical systems leave observable records such as certificates, public services,

00:00:50.792 --> 00:00:52.029
and software characteristics.

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:56.150
These traces matter because they affect privacy, security, safety, reputation,

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:56.974
and investigations.

00:00:56.974 --> 00:00:59.035
One detail may seem harmless,

00:00:59.035 --> 00:01:03.156
but several accurate details can combine into a sensitive picture.

00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:09.338
Old or incorrect information can also create risk when it is treated as current fact.

00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:13.459
Legitimate defensive analysis can identify unnecessary exposure, support incident response,

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:16.344
verify organizational assets, and improve privacy controls.

00:01:16.344 --> 00:01:19.641
It should be bounded by purpose, authority, proportionality,

00:01:19.641 --> 00:01:22.938
and respect for people affected by the information.

00:01:22.938 --> 00:01:27.884
A digital footprint is not a complete identity or a guaranteed truth.

00:01:27.884 --> 00:01:33.654
It is a changing set of observable traces that must be interpreted in context.

00:01:33.654 --> 00:01:36.539
Responsible work validates sources, minimizes personal data,

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:40.660
and uses findings to reduce risk rather than exploit individuals.
